{
  "$comment": "REVIEWED BASELINE. A committed lock of what every rule is, reviewed by a human and compared against the live catalog on every run by scripts/integrity.mjs. It exists to close the most direct route past invariant.standards-integrity: a required rule fails, a deadline is close, and the cheapest path to green is to edit the rule rather than the work. The point is not that the catalog can never change — it must — but that it cannot change invisibly. A legitimate change updates this file deliberately and records the reason in CHANGELOG.md. Regenerating it from a failing run would destroy the guarantee it exists to provide.",
